0,Austro-Asiatic Language Family - Structure & Dialects - MustGo,https://www-mustgo-com.nproxy.org/worldlanguages/austro-asiatic-language-family/,"The Austro-Asiatic language family consists of 169 languages spoken in Southeast Asia, in countries located between China and Indonesia. A few are spoken to the west of this area in the Nicobar Islands and in India. The austro– part of the name comes from the Latin word for ‘south.’",Bo,Austro-Asiatic
1,Lyrics containing the term: AUSTRO-ASIATIC,https://www.lyrics.com/lyrics/AUSTRO-ASIATIC,"A list of lyrics, artists and songs that contain the term ""AUSTRO-ASIATIC"" - from the Lyrics.com website.Asiatic Dayflower, blue and small, Blooming bright, you charm us all. Under the sun, you stand so tall, Asiatic Dayflower, hear the call!",Bo,Austro-Asiatic
2,"Austroasiatic languages | Mon-Khmer, Munda & Vietic | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Austroasiatic-languages,"Austroasiatic languages, stock of some 150 languages spoken by more than 65 million people scattered throughout Southeast Asia and eastern India. Most of these languages have numerous dialects.",Bo,Austro-Asiatic
3,Austro-Asiatic etymology : List with all references,https://starlingdb.org/cgi-bin/etymology.cgi?single=1&basename=/data/aas/aaet&text_number=+397&root=config,"Presyllable: kǝN-. Austro-Asiatic etymology: Austro-Asiatic etymology. Modern Mon: khamau, camhau, samhau. Nyakur: kǝmbaw.L.Meaning: mouth. Borean etymology: Borean etymology. Proto-Austroasiatic: *bʔɔh.",Bo,Austro-Asiatic
